description:
lib.rs:1239-1273 LintRunner::new and lib.rs:1305-1316 LintRunner::with_bundle_version both call Self::check_unique_ids and both construct the struct field-by-field with a different bundle_version literal. The two constructors are 95% identical.

Future readers (including the maintainer in 12 months) will read this and wonder 'why two functions doing the same thing'. The fix is mechanical:

  pub fn new(lints) -> Self { Self::with_bundle_version(lints, '') }
  pub fn with_bundle_version(lints, version) -> Self { ... }

This makes new() a single-line forwarder and locks in the invariant that the two constructors enforce the same precondition.

Minor — flagged because the duplication is in a public API that has explicit panic semantics; the duplication is the kind of thing that quietly diverges across a refactor.
